SUMMARY:Computational phenotypes: traits\, states\, or moving targets? — 
 Emory Decision-Making Megalab
DESCRIPTION:Article discussion. At our September 25 meeting\, we discussed 
 individual differences\, repeated measurement\, parameter stability\, and 
 what makes a useful computational phenotype\, drawing on Schurr et al. (20
 24) and the companion paper by Katahira\, Oba & Toyama (2024). Featured ar
 ticle: Dynamic computational phenotyping of human cognition. Authors: Schu
 rr\, Reznik\, Hillman\, Bhui\, et al.. Journal: Nature Human Behaviour (20
 24). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-024-01814-x Featured article: Does the
  reliability of computational models truly improve with hierarchical model
 ing? Some recommendations and considerations for the assessment of model p
 arameter reliability. Authors: Katahira\, Oba & Toyama. Journal: Psychonom
 ic Bulletin & Review (2024). https://doi.org/10.3758/s13423-024-02490-8 Le
 ad: Michael Hallquist. Location: PAIS 280.
LOCATION:PAIS 280
